camera2: report 3A state in results and zoom metadata in characteristics

Instagram's camera (Optic) registered the shutter tap and never took the photo.
The capture task died on list.get(0) of an empty zoom-ratio list: the device
advertised no SCALER_AVAILABLE_MAX_DIGITAL_ZOOM, so Optic took it for a camera
without zoom metadata. camera2 requires that key of every device (>= 1.0) and,
from API 30, CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO_RANGE; AOSP's legacy shim reports 1.0 for a camera
without zoom. Both are now advertised as [1.0, 1.0], with SCALER_CROPPING_TYPE
CENTER_ONLY.

Each capture result now also carries the 3A state camera2 requires of every
device, as AOSP's LegacyResultMapper fills it for a LEGACY camera: AE CONVERGED
(PRECAPTURE on the frame carrying the trigger), AF INACTIVE (fixed focus), AWB
CONVERGED, FLASH UNAVAILABLE, LENS STATIONARY, and the request's AE/AF modes and
triggers echoed back.

Measured (Instagram 455, Logitech C922): the shutter takes a 1920x1080 JPEG and
the Story editor opens with it.

diff --git a/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraBackend.java b/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraBackend.java
--- a/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraBackend.java
+++ b/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraBackend.java
@@ -285,6 +285,19 @@ final class CameraBackend {
                     new Rect(0, 0, fmt.maxWidth, fmt.maxHeight));
         }
 
+        // Zoom: none, said the way camera2 says it. SCALER_AVAILABLE_MAX_DIGITAL_ZOOM
+        // is present on every device (>= 1.0); AOSP's legacy shim reports 1.0
+        // for a camera without zoom, and from API 30 CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO_RANGE is
+        // [1.0, that maximum]. Absent, Instagram's camera (Optic) took the
+        // camera for one without zoom metadata at all, left its zoom-ratio list
+        // empty and failed every photo on list.get(0) (IndexOutOfBounds inside
+        // the capture task, measured 2026-11-12).
+        p.put(CameraCharacteristics.SCALER_AVAILABLE_MAX_DIGITAL_ZOOM, Float.valueOf(1f));
+        p.put(CameraCharacteristics.CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO_RANGE,
+                new android.util.Range<>(Float.valueOf(1f), Float.valueOf(1f)));
+        p.put(CameraCharacteristics.SCALER_CROPPING_TYPE,
+                Integer.valueOf(CameraMetadata.SCALER_CROPPING_TYPE_CENTER_ONLY));
+
         // Deliberately ABSENT: LENS_INFO_AVAILABLE_FOCAL_LENGTHS and
         // SENSOR_INFO_PHYSICAL_SIZE. AVFoundation does not tell us the focal
         // length or the sensor's physical dimensions, and those two are
@@ -312,6 +326,17 @@ final class CameraBackend {
         // that is the whole honest list.
         List<CaptureResult.Key<?>> resultKeys = new ArrayList<>();
         resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.SENSOR_TIMESTAMP);
+        // The 3A state this LEGACY, fixed-focus, always-auto-exposure device has
+        // (CameraCaptureSessionImpl fills them in each result).
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_STATE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_STATE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AWB_STATE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.FLASH_STATE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.LENS_STATE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_MODE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_MODE);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_PRECAPTURE_TRIGGER);
+        resultKeys.add(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_TRIGGER);
 
         trace("characteristics id=" + cameraId + " index=" + index
                 + " unique=" + unique
diff --git a/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraCaptureSessionImpl.java b/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraCaptureSessionImpl.java
--- a/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraCaptureSessionImpl.java
+++ b/runtime/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraCaptureSessionImpl.java
@@ -1023,14 +1111,39 @@ final class CameraCaptureSessionImpl extends CameraCaptureSession {
 
         dispatch.run(() -> cb.onCaptureStarted(this, req, timestampNs, deliveredCount));
 
-        // The result carries only what we measured. SENSOR_TIMESTAMP is the
-        // observation instant described above; exposure time, sensitivity and
-        // the 3A states are absent because AVFoundation does not report them
-        // per frame through this path, and a plausible-looking fabricated value
-        // is worse than a null an app can test for. CameraCharacteristics
-        // .getAvailableCaptureResultKeys() advertises exactly this one key.
+        // SENSOR_TIMESTAMP is the observation instant described above. Exposure
+        // time and sensitivity stay absent (AVFoundation does not report them per
+        // frame through this path). The 3A STATE is reported, because camera2
+        // requires it of every device -- AOSP's legacy shim fills it for a LEGACY
+        // camera too (LegacyResultMapper) -- and a capture flow waits on it: a
+        // precapture sequence waits for AE_STATE to leave PRECAPTURE, and with
+        // the keys absent Instagram's camera registered the shutter tap and
+        // never took the picture (measured 2026-11-12). This device is what
+        // CameraBackend advertises: fixed focus (AF mode OFF -> INACTIVE),
+        // auto-exposure always on and run by AVFoundation (CONVERGED; PRECAPTURE
+        // on the frame that carries the trigger, as the shim does), AWB
+        // CONVERGED, no flash (UNAVAILABLE), lens STATIONARY. Modes and
+        // triggers are echoed from the request, as AOSP results carry them.
         Map<CaptureResult.Key<?>, Object> results = new HashMap<>();
         results.put(CaptureResult.SENSOR_TIMESTAMP, Long.valueOf(timestampNs));
+        if (req != null) {
+            final Integer aeTrigger = req.get(CaptureRequest.CONTROL_AE_PRECAPTURE_TRIGGER);
+            final boolean precapture = aeTrigger != null
+                    && aeTrigger.intValue() == CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AE_PRECAPTURE_TRIGGER_START;
+            results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_STATE, Integer.valueOf(precapture
+                    ? CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AE_STATE_PRECAPTURE : CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AE_STATE_CONVERGED));
+            results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_STATE, Integer.valueOf(CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AF_STATE_INACTIVE));
+            results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AWB_STATE, Integer.valueOf(CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AWB_STATE_CONVERGED));
+            results.put(CaptureResult.FLASH_STATE, Integer.valueOf(CameraMetadata.FLASH_STATE_UNAVAILABLE));
+            results.put(CaptureResult.LENS_STATE, Integer.valueOf(CameraMetadata.LENS_STATE_STATIONARY));
+            final Integer aeMode = req.get(CaptureRequest.CONTROL_AE_MODE);
+            if (aeMode != null) results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_MODE, aeMode);
+            final Integer afMode = req.get(CaptureRequest.CONTROL_AF_MODE);
+            if (afMode != null) results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_MODE, afMode);
+            if (aeTrigger != null) results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AE_PRECAPTURE_TRIGGER, aeTrigger);
+            final Integer afTrigger = req.get(CaptureRequest.CONTROL_AF_TRIGGER);
+            if (afTrigger != null) results.put(CaptureResult.CONTROL_AF_TRIGGER, afTrigger);
+        }
         final TotalCaptureResult result = new TotalCaptureResult(results, req, deliveredCount,
                 mDevice.getId(), seq);
 
